moose-ripple @VERSION@ for Mac OS X 10.6.8 (alpha)
====================================================

GPU acceleration for Snow Leopard in QEMU: Quartz Extreme, OpenGL 2.1 and Core Image on the
host's GPU through virtio-gpu and virgl. Project page and full instructions:
https://github.com/mizaimao/moose-ripple

Before you start
- The VM runs Mac OS X 10.6.8 with the 64-bit kernel, booted by OpenCore, with QEMU's
  virtio-vga-gl card (Proxmox: vga: virtio-gl). The VM settings are in the project's README.
- Turn sleep off in the guest: sudo pmset -a sleep 0 displaysleep 0 disksleep 0
- Take a snapshot of the VM.

Install
1. Get this folder into the guest. Snow Leopard can't download from GitHub, so on the host
   make a CD image of the unpacked folder and attach it to the VM:
     genisoimage -V RIPPLE -r -J -o ripple.iso moose-ripple-@VERSION@
2. In the guest's Terminal:
     cd /Volumes/RIPPLE
     sudo sh install.sh                (or: sudo sh install.sh --no-tablet)
3. Restart: sudo reboot

Check
- The menu bar is translucent. F12, then drag a widget onto the Dashboard: the water ripples.
- /Volumes/RIPPLE/qe-check prints "QE on" for each display.

Remove
     sudo sh uninstall.sh
     sudo reboot

Files
  RippleVirtioGPU.kext    display and GPU driver (kernel)
  RippleGLDriver.bundle   OpenGL driver (Mesa's virgl driver for 10.6)
  RippleGA.plugin         2D plugin WindowServer needs before it composites with OpenGL
  RippleQEMUTablet.kext   optional: the pointer follows QEMU's USB tablet exactly
  qe-check                prints whether each display has Quartz Extreme
  install.sh, uninstall.sh, INSTALL, LICENSE, LICENSE-Mesa.rst
  SHA256SUMS              checksums of all the above: shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS

Mac OS X itself is not included and must come from your own copy. moose-ripple is MIT
licensed (LICENSE). RippleGLDriver.bundle contains Mesa, under Mesa's own licenses
(LICENSE-Mesa.rst).
